# WLISTT.KEY - the key script of the list window's test, TEST/WLISTT.C,
# run by "WIN WLISTT TDATA /KEYS:WLISTT.KEY /SNAP:WLISTT.SNP" on the
# seeded data; every mode of Windows writes TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTT.SNP.
# The list's window holds two rows, so the three items take two pages.
# The title's count shows which moves were busy.
S START
# DOWN within the window, sending nothing, then out of it: the window
# moves a row.
K DOWN
S DOWN
K DOWN
S DOWN2
# DOWN on the last row stays.
K DOWN
S LAST
K PGUP
S PGUP
K PGDN
S PGDN
K HOME
S HOME
# END walks to the last page and ends the window on its last row.
K END
S END
# TAB changes the order and the header, SHIFT-TAB is the owner's, and
# TAB wraps back to the first order.
K HOME TAB
S SERIAL
K SHIFT-TAB
S STAB
K TAB
S ID
# A click on the second row selects it without a request; a double
# click on the first selects it and opens it.
K F2
S CLICK
K SHIFT-F3
S DBLCLK
# F5 sets the selected item's quantity and reloads.
K DOWN F5
S RELOAD
K ENTER
S OPEN
# A character typed is dropped; a key the owner does not take comes to
# it with SHIFT and CTRL.
T 3
S CHAR
K CTRL-INS
S KEY
# An Esc waiting when END starts stops its walk.
K HOME F7
S STOPPED
# F6 filters every item out: the empty text; F6 again brings them back.
K F6
S EMPTY
K F6
S FULL
# A filter the server refuses: its box, after which the list stays.
K F8
S REFUSED
K ENTER
S STAYED
K F8
S BACK
# F9 ends the session and reloads: the failure's box, whose action,
# after ENTER, makes the owner destroy the list; ESC then ends.
K F9
S ENDED
K ENTER
S LEFT
K ESC
S GONE
